**How to implement.** The column-mapping wizard's pure MVU: it opens on a picked file, shows how its layout reads, takes a built-in or kit profile or a new column mapping, and on Attach hands the kit window the profile to attach by and the new profile to save (001 §K 'Column-mapping import wizard'; 001 §O 'Data dialog: preview, column roles, an import-profile picker'; the S9.2 brief: its own view and window; .spec-md §10.3 identify → confirm: nothing is attached or saved until Attach; the shape of step 107's import dialog). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView`, compiled directly after `SetupGridView.fs` (step 283), before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment; the module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §K and spec 0050 S9.2, and every type, case and field has a one-line doc. (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ImportWizardRequest = { experimentId : Experiments.ExperimentId; file : FileName; readPickedFile : FileName -> Result<LabFileSource, KitError>; kitProfiles : ImportProfile list; defaultProfile : ImportProfileName }`: what the kit window hands the wizard (step 310). (2) `ImportWizardApplied = { experimentId : Experiments.ExperimentId; file : FileName; profile : ImportProfileName; savedOpt : ImportProfile option }`: what Attach chose, the profile to attach the file by and the new profile to save first. (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ImportWizardContext = { request : ImportWizardRequest; onApplied : ImportWizardApplied -> unit; requestClose : unit -> unit }`, in the shape of `ImportDialogContext` (step 107). (4) `WizardProfileChoice` = `PickedImportProfile of ImportProfileName` | `NewColumnMapping`. (5) `ImportWizardModel = { context : ImportWizardContext; source : Result<LabFileSource, KitError>; delimiter : DataDelimiter; header : HeaderRowChoice; bom : ByteOrderMark; choice : WizardProfileChoice; columns : ColumnChoice list; profileName : ControlCaption; lastError : ImportProfileError option }`, with `member this.preview : Result<LabFilePreview, ExperimentDataError>`: the source's `content.kitFileText.previewWith delimiter header` (step 307), or `MalformedDataFileErr` of the read's `describe`. (6) `initImportWizard (context : ImportWizardContext) : ImportWizardModel` reads `context.request.readPickedFile context.request.file`, its one read; an `Ok` source takes its `sniffedLayout` (step 307), any error the comma, a header row and no mark; the choice is `PickedImportProfile context.request.defaultProfile`; `columns` is one `UnmappedColumnRole` choice per column of the preview, numbered from 1 (none when the preview failed); the name is empty and there is no error. (7) `ImportWizardMsg`, each case documented: `SetImportDelimiter of DataDelimiter`, `SetImportHeader of HeaderRowChoice`, `PickImportProfile of ImportProfileName`, `StartColumnMapping`, `SetColumnRole of DataColumnNumber * ColumnRoleChoice`, `SetImportProfileName of ControlCaption`, `ApplyImportWizard` and `CancelImportWizard`. (8) `updateImportWizard (msg : ImportWizardMsg) (m : ImportWizardModel) : ImportWizardModel`. `SetImportDelimiter` and `SetImportHeader` set the layout and remake `columns` over the new preview, each column number that remains keeping its role and a new one `UnmappedColumnRole`. `PickImportProfile name` takes the choice `PickedImportProfile name` when `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName request.kitProfiles name` (step 300) resolves it, a kit profile also setting the layout to its delimiter, header and mark, and is inert otherwise. `StartColumnMapping` takes `NewColumnMapping`. `SetColumnRole (column, role)` replaces that column's role and takes `NewColumnMapping`, and is inert for a column the model lacks. `SetImportProfileName` sets the name. Each of these clears `lastError`. `ApplyImportWizard` is the only message that reaches the context, and is inert while the source is an error: under `PickedImportProfile name` it calls `onApplied { experimentId; file; profile = name; savedOpt = None }` and then `requestClose ()`; under `NewColumnMapping` it takes `ImportProfileName.tryCreate profileName.value` (step 291; `None` is `BlankProfileNameErr` `the profile name is empty`), its `availableAmong request.kitProfiles` (step 299) and `ColumnRoles.tryOfChoices columns` (step 300), and the first error sets `lastError` and applies nothing, while success calls `onApplied` with the profile's name and `savedOpt = Some { name; delimiter; header; bom; roles }`, then `requestClose ()`. `CancelImportWizard` calls `requestClose ()` and nothing else. No other message, option or seam is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs`, `module ImportWizardTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended to the compile list after `ImportDialogTests.fs` with no comment, over a recording context: its request's `experimentId` is `ExperimentId 1`, its `file` a test-local name, its `readPickedFile` answers the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\n`, its `kitProfiles` hold `Lab scan` (step 299's fixture, written test-locally) and its `defaultProfile` is `Intensity series`; `onApplied` and `requestClose` are recorded. `the wizard opens on the picked file with its sniffed layout and the detector's profile chosen`: `initImportWizard` holds `CommaDelimiter`, `HeaderOnFirstRow`, `ByteOrderMarkPresent`, `PickedImportProfile` of `Intensity series` and five `UnmappedColumnRole` columns numbered 1 to 5. `picking a profile, changing the layout or mapping a column changes nothing outside the wizard`: `PickImportProfile` of `Phone ROI CSV` takes it, of `Lab scan` also sets the layout to `Lab scan`'s, and of `Nope` is inert; `SetImportDelimiter SemicolonDelimiter` leaves one column; and no `onApplied` or close is recorded. `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes`: `PickImportProfile` of `Phone ROI CSV` then `ApplyImportWizard` records one `onApplied` of `ExperimentId 1`, the file, `Phone ROI CSV` and `None`, then one close. `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it`: `SetColumnRole` of column 1 `KeyColumnRole`, 2 `CaptureIndexColumnRole`, 3 `TimestampColumnRole`, 4 `ScanColumnRole (DegreeColumnUnit, RawDialReading)` and 5 `SignalColumnRole`, `SetImportProfileName (ControlCaption "Phone ROI by columns")` and `ApplyImportWizard` record one `onApplied` whose `profile` is `Phone ROI by columns` and whose `savedOpt` holds a profile of comma, a header row, the mark, scan column 4 in degrees as a raw dial reading, `SignalColumns (5, None)`, timestamp 3, capture index 2 and key 1, then one close. `a mapping that cannot be a profile is told and nothing is applied`: Attach with an empty name sets `BlankProfileNameErr`, with the name `Intensity series` `BuiltInProfileNameErr`, with `Lab scan` `DuplicateProfileNameErr` and with two signal columns `SignalColumnCountErr`, each recording no `onApplied` and no close. `a picked file that cannot be read offers only Cancel, and Cancel applies nothing`: over a `readPickedFile` answering `KitIoErr`, the source is that error, the model has no column, `ApplyImportWizard` records nothing, and `CancelImportWizard` records one close and no `onApplied`.

**Acceptance.** After the wizard's MVU lands, `ImportWizardView` MUST open on a picked file's sniffed layout with the detector's profile chosen and reach its context only on `ApplyImportWizard`, handing the kit window the chosen profile and any new mapping as a profile to save, with a refused mapping told; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the wizard opens on the picked file with its sniffed layout and the detector's profile chosen`, `picking a profile, changing the layout or mapping a column changes nothing outside the wizard`, `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes`, `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it`, `a mapping that cannot be a profile is told and nothing is applied` and `a picked file that cannot be read offers only Cancel, and Cancel applies nothing`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
